},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 40\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 48\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1989). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Flint's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Flint has set <strong>75 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 93 that chance alone would give, and <strong>100 record highs</strong>, close to the 93 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (85). Flint's all-time high is 108\u00b0F, on July 8, 1936.","t_chg":"Flint's nights have warmed. Its days have warmed since 1986.","p_chg":"Across 104 complete years: Flint's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.10\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.00 to +0.20), about +1.1\u00b0F since 1921. Flint's average high shows no clear change: +0.02\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.10 to +0.14) that includes zero. July and August highs have edged down across the full record; the 1930s summers were the hottest in it. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.60\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +1.01) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.67\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.22 to +1.11). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 1 of 12 months; July and August fell.","t_rain":"Flint has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Flint's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.40 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.04 to +0.77), about +4.2 inches since 1921. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 31.9 inches a year. The wettest year was 1975 (45.38 in); the driest, 1963 (18.08 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 6 daily record highs, 3 daily record lows"}}